WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.800
These are dark times for The Darkest Minds.

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:08.260
Over the first weekend of August 2018, the
YA series turned hopeful film franchise was

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:12.880
introduced to moviegoers by 20th Century Fox
- and audiences were not interested.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:19.280
Released in 3,127 theaters, the movie was
met with a resounding splat at the box office,

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.900
earning only around $6 million domestically
and not faring much better overseas.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.900
It's enough to mark the movie as having one
of the worst opening weekends ever for a release

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.600
of that size - so you can probably say goodbye
to any adaptation of the series' second book.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.060
What happened to make this adaptation fail
where others have soared?

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.220
Why did The Darkest Minds bomb at the box
office?

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.920
Follow our signal - we have the answers that
you seek.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.620
Colorful characters

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.120
Considering how few people went to see it,
it might be best to recap what The Darkest

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:49.120
Minds even is.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.829
Based on a book series by Alexandra Bracken,
the film centers on a near-future apocalypse

00:00:53.829 --> 00:00:58.080
in which the vast majority of children in
the US contract a mysterious disease.

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.800
While the illness kills most people, the lucky
survivors are gifted with immense powers,

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.920
with their eyes glowing a certain color depending
on what they can do.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:11.020
Greens are very intelligent, blues are telekinetic,
and golds can control electricity.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:15.430
The most powerful are the oranges, who can
control minds, and the reds, who control fire.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:18.860
The powerful survivors are seen as such a
threat that they're ripped away from their

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:23.530
families and placed into internment camps,
with the most powerful kids either being enlisted

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:26.900
by authorities as government enforcers or
outright killed.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.880
The main character is Ruby Daly, a powerful
orange who disguises herself as a green for

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:32.520
her own survival.

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:37.300
When her true nature is exposed, she flees
her camp with the help of a sympathetic doctor

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:40.280
and sets off with other runaways in search
of a safe haven.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.240
Muddled marketing

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.420
So the plot sounds simple, right?

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:46.850
Good kids with powers on the run from bad
adults.

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:50.140
But the movie's marketing team didn't manage
to convey any of that.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:55.200
Instead, ads made the story look like "a Nicholas
Sparks adaptation meets the climax of Avengers:

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:55.980
Infinity War".

00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:00.100
A more action-oriented trailer made it seem
like the cheapest X-Men movie yet.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.270
In all the marketing materials, the premise
is under explained, only resonating if you're

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:06.140
already familiar with the source material.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.689
It raises the question: Who are these promos
meant to attract?

00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:12.000
Whatever the campaign was going for - it didn't
work.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.080
Give it some star power

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.840
When it comes to this movie's cast, even the
casual viewer is probably going to recognize

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.620
the likes of Mandy Moore, Bradley Whitford,
and Gwendoline Christie.

00:02:22.829 --> 00:02:26.279
The problem is, these recognizable actors
aren't the movie's leads.

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:30.109
Instead, the heavy promotional lifting for
The Darkest Minds was left to the younger

00:02:30.109 --> 00:02:34.549
kids in the cast, none of whom have really
established themselves as marketable draws

00:02:34.549 --> 00:02:37.239
at this point in their careers, despite their
talents.

00:02:37.239 --> 00:02:41.769
The closest the film has to a young breakout
star is Amandla Stenberg as main character

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:45.239
Ruby, evoking memories of her turn as Rue
in The Hunger Games.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.360
But as far as name actors go, that's it.

00:02:47.529 --> 00:02:51.680
This is like if they tried to sell the Jumanji
sequel with the actors who played the students

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.669
instead of Dwayne Johnson and company.

00:02:53.669 --> 00:02:57.880
When it comes to box office performance, the
lack of familiar faces certainly didn't help.

00:02:58.640 --> 00:02:59.760
Murky action

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.319
As several reviews for The Darkest Minds have
pointed out, the movie didn't impress when

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:08.060
it comes to its action sequences, which have
been described as incoherent.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:13.010
The Darkest Minds is directed by Jennifer
Yuh Nelson, an Emmy award-winning storyboard

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:18.140
artist and filmmaker who was previously up
for an Oscar for directing Kung Fu Panda 2.

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:22.840
Though she's worked in animation for decades
now, The Darkest Minds is only her third feature

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.819
as director, and her very first live-action
project.

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:30.760
While the movie's premise has drawn comparisons
to the X-Men movies, The Darkest Minds can't

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:35.040
hold a candle to that franchise's often inventive,
adrenaline-pumping set pieces.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.440
A version of the X-Men with only the social
commentary and none of the spectacle is…

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.560
well, kind of a lousy version of the X-Men.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:46.140
A lack of action-packed sequences makes it
harder to sell the movie to audiences wanting

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:50.729
superhero-style thrills, contributing to what
made this project such a weak draw at the

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:55.159
box office, and made so many people head over
to catch the fifth weekend run of Ant-Man

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.120
and the Wasp instead.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:57.760
Cut-rate

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.080
Other reviews of The Darkest Minds have described
the movie as having the look of a CW pilot

00:04:03.089 --> 00:04:05.889
which, while charming, have a tendency to
look pretty cheap.

00:04:05.889 --> 00:04:10.180
Put simply, The Darkest Minds is not the kind
of production that is flattered by a big-screen

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:10.880
presentation.

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:15.839
With a reported budget of $34 million, The
Darkest Minds clearly didn't have a lot of

00:04:15.839 --> 00:04:20.009
money to throw around, leaving the movie looking
every bit like the inexpensive production

00:04:20.009 --> 00:04:20.509
it is.

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:24.840
This isn't necessarily a bad thing, but why
trek out to the movie theater when you can

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.940
pull up some straight-to-Netflix silliness
that looks just as good, or even better?

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:30.800
Twilight of YA

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:35.740
One of Hollywood's biggest trends in the last
decade has been the explosion of adaptations

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.380
of young adult properties from the well-known
to the unknown.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:39.860
You know the ones we're talking about.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:41.240
"Since when do vampires like baseball?"

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:42.840
"Well—"

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:47.539
After the titanic success of the Harry Potter
movies, school bookshelves were picked clean

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:51.629
by industry producers, all looking for the
next big property that the kids can't stop

00:04:51.629 --> 00:04:52.340
talking about.

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:56.880
But while that trend was once dominant, it's
now clearly receding, which makes The Darkest

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.040
Minds feel shockingly late to the party.

00:04:59.260 --> 00:05:00.840
Worse, it has nothing new to say.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.980
The darkest legacy

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.020
While The Darkest Minds is facing a terrible
opening weekend with abysmal reviews, the

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:10.920
actual long-term damage is not quite as bad
as you might think.

00:05:11.180 --> 00:05:13.940
Given time, the movie may actually end up
making money.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:18.300
With its small budget in mind, there actually
is still an avenue for The Darkest Minds to

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.320
make money through home media sales and syndication.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.300
In the long run, that's a success.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:27.520
Unfortunately, despite ending with a crushing
sequel hook that leaves a main character's

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:31.610
life in the balance, the odds of seeing The
Darkest Minds continue forward on the big

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:32.610
screen are slim.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:33.990
But things could have gone a lot worse.

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:37.340
This story may seem over, but it's not necessarily
a tragedy.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:41.660
Something tells us that this talented cast
at least will walk away from this soft opening

00:05:41.669 --> 00:05:43.069
relatively unscathed.

